The battery's reading for an app: plat_battery_raw() (include/plat.h), the smoothed 10-bit reading on the battery's
divider that plat_battery's bars come from (device/plat_fm1.c's batt_raw, read ten times a second by the main loop).
The host simulator gives 640, or what "battery RAW" sets.
And a fix to that reading's average (device/main_fm1.c): batt_raw + (b - batt_raw) / 16 never moved for a difference
under 16 (the division rounds it to 0), so the reading stayed near its first value until the next power-on, and the
bars with it. The average is kept x16 now (batt_q4), so a small change adds up.
Why MIDIMON needs it: a battery percentage (GLO 1/3) that follows the battery, not only the stock firmware's bars.
Applies to: fm1-base aa2b3bc, after 0001-0003. Upstream: not offered yet.
diff --git a/device/main_fm1.c b/device/main_fm1.c
index fd1aeb3..6b9793e 100644
--- a/device/main_fm1.c
+++ b/device/main_fm1.c
@@ -880,8 +880,11 @@ static void fm1_main(void)
         if (!fm1_an.con && !fm1_an.pend && fm1_ms - batt_t >= 100u) {   /* the battery, ten times a second (plat_battery) */
             int32_t b = fm1_adc_read(FM1_ADC_BATT);
             batt_t = fm1_ms;
-            if (b > 0)
-                batt_raw = batt_raw ? batt_raw + (b - batt_raw) / 16 : b;
+            if (b > 0) {                            /* a sixteenth of the way each time, kept x16: the plain
+                                                     * (b - batt_raw) / 16 never moved for a difference under 16 */
+                batt_q4 = batt_q4 ? batt_q4 + b - (batt_q4 + 8) / 16 : b * 16;
+                batt_raw = (batt_q4 + 8) / 16;
+            }
         }
         fm1b_dbg.stage = 2;                         /* (breadcrumbs: where a watchdog reset found the loop) */
         ble_poll();                                 /* Bluetooth's tasks, once started */
